		"name": "ToDo Microservice API",
		"description": "Complete API collection for testing the ToDo microservice.\n\nThis collection includes all available endpoints:\n- Health checks (liveness and readiness probes)\n- CRUD operations for ToDo items\n\n**Base URL Options:**\n- Local: http://localhost:8080\n- Docker: http://localhost:8080\n- Kubernetes (port-forward): http://localhost:8080\n\n**Usage:**\n1. Update the {{baseUrl}} variable to match your environment\n2. Run requests in order to see full workflow\n3. The collection uses variables to store created IDs automatically",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "Health Checks",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Liveness Probe",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health/live",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"health",
								"live"
							]
						},
						"description": "Check if the service is alive and running.\n\n**Expected Response:**\n- Status: 200 OK\n- Body: \"OK\"\n\n**Use Case:**\nKubernetes uses this endpoint to determine if the pod should be restarted."
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Readiness Probe",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health/ready",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"health",
								"ready"
							]
						},
						"description": "Check if the service is ready to accept traffic.\n\n**Expected Response:**\n- Status: 200 OK (when ready)\n- Status: 503 Service Unavailable (when not ready)\n- Body: \"OK\" or \"Not Ready\"\n\n**Use Case:**\nKubernetes uses this endpoint to determine if traffic should be routed to the pod."
					},
					"response": []
				}
			],
			"description": "Health check endpoints for Kubernetes probes."
		},
		{
			"name": "ToDo Operations",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Get All Todos",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test(\"Response is an array\", function () {",
									"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData).to.be.an('array');",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test(\"Content-Type is application/json\", function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.header(\"Content-Type\");",
									"    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get(\"Content-Type\")).to.include(\"application/json\");",
									"});"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/todos",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"todos"
							]
						},
						"description": "Retrieve all todo items.\n\n**Expected Response:**\n- Status: 200 OK\n- Body: Array of todo objects\n\n**Response Schema:**\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"uuid\",\n    \"title\": \"string\",\n    \"completed\": boolean\n  }\n]\n```\n\n**Empty List:**\nReturns empty array [] when no todos exist."
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Create Todo - Example 1",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"Status code is 201\", function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test(\"Response has id, title, and completed fields\", function () {",
									"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('id');",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('title');",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('completed');",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test(\"Todo is not completed by default\", function () {",
									"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData.completed).to.be.false;",
									"});",
									"",
									"// Save the ID for later use",
									"var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set(\"todoId1\", jsonData.id);"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Learn Go programming\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/todos",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"todos"
							]
						},
						"description": "Create a new todo item.\n\n**Request Body:**\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"string\" (required)\n}\n```\n\n**Expected Response:**\n- Status: 201 Created\n- Body: Created todo object with generated UUID\n\n**Response Schema:**\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"uuid\",\n  \"title\": \"string\",\n  \"completed\": false\n}\n```\n\n**Error Cases:**\n- 400 Bad Request: Missing or empty title\n- 400 Bad Request: Invalid JSON format"
					},
					"response": []
				},
